  A plain [38;5;153m<input type="checkbox">[39m wrapped in a [38;5;153m<label>[39m, so the text is clickable too. The browser handles the on/off
  state natively — no JS needed for that. Nothing else in the file changed.

  One thing worth flagging: this is a single static checkbox. The page has no task list yet, so there's nothing to mark
  done per-item. When you add tasks, you'll want one checkbox per item (rendered in a loop) plus somewhere to persist
  the checked state — that's a larger design step than this edit.

